Let us write measured household assets as $A_{\mathrm{hh}}$, measured household liabilities as $L_{\mathrm{hh}}$, and net worth as $NW_{\mathrm{hh}}$. The slide gives the core accounting identity directly: $\begin{aligned}
NW_{\mathrm{hh}}
  &= A_{\mathrm{hh}} - L_{\mathrm{hh}} \\
  &= 70{,}740 - 13{,}918 \\
  &= 56{,}822,\end{aligned}$ where the units are billions of dollars.

